WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.700 --> 00:00:06.719
Three picks reach a search box, 100 milliseconds apart.

2
00:00:06.719 --> 00:00:12.493
Each pick starts an inner flow: part a after 50 milliseconds, part b 150 later.

3
00:00:12.493 --> 00:00:15.051
The flatMaps differ in their lanes.

4
00:00:15.667 --> 00:00:17.544
flatMapConcat has one lane.

5
00:00:17.544 --> 00:00:20.117
When does the outer flow emit pick 2?

6
00:00:22.600 --> 00:00:23.431
Not at 100.

7
00:00:23.431 --> 00:00:30.156
The inner flow runs inside the outer's emit, so the outer is stuck until inner 1 is done.

8
00:00:30.156 --> 00:00:32.498
Only then does its delay start.

9
00:00:32.498 --> 00:00:35.747
Pick 2 comes at 300, and the run takes 800.

10
00:00:36.467 --> 00:00:40.481
flatMapMerge gives each inner flow its own lane.

11
00:00:40.481 --> 00:00:47.003
Picks come at 0, 100 and 200, and values come out as they finish: 1b after 2a.

12
00:00:47.003 --> 00:00:48.007
Done at 400.

13
00:00:48.733 --> 00:00:51.409
flatMapLatest has one lane and a switch.

14
00:00:51.409 --> 00:00:57.364
A new pick cancels the inner flow in the lane, waits for it to stop, and starts the next.

15
00:00:57.364 --> 00:00:58.902
1b and 2b never arrive.

16
00:00:58.902 --> 00:01:01.645
That is the shape for search as you type.

17
00:01:02.467 --> 00:01:03.933
Now a fee fan-out.

18
00:01:03.933 --> 00:01:12.326
Five lookups take 300, 100, 200, 50 and 150 milliseconds, and the fee service allows two calls at once.

19
00:01:12.326 --> 00:01:16.807
A teammate calls the lookup in the flatMapMerge lambda.

20
00:01:16.807 --> 00:01:18.600
How long does it take?

21
00:01:21.100 --> 00:01:23.605
800 milliseconds, one call at a time.

22
00:01:23.605 --> 00:01:29.562
The lambda runs in the one coroutine that reads the merchants, before any lane is taken.

23
00:01:29.562 --> 00:01:34.233
Picture a toll plaza where the dispatcher inspects every car himself.

24
00:01:34.233 --> 00:01:35.655
The booths sit empty.

25
00:01:36.267 --> 00:01:39.264
Move the lookup inside the flow you return.

26
00:01:39.264 --> 00:01:44.283
Now the dispatcher only waves cars in, and the lookups run in the lanes.

27
00:01:44.283 --> 00:01:46.166
Two at a time, done at 450.

28
00:01:46.166 --> 00:01:49.093
Results come out as they finish, m2 first.

29
00:01:49.900 --> 00:01:52.831
The slow call goes inside the returned flow.

30
00:01:52.831 --> 00:01:58.425
Reactor has the same trap: block in the mapper, and flatMap runs one call at a time.

31
00:01:59.900 --> 00:02:03.689
So flatMapConcat runs one lane and makes the outer wait.

32
00:02:03.689 --> 00:02:06.734
flatMapMerge gives each returned flow a lane.

33
00:02:06.734 --> 00:02:10.117
flatMapLatest keeps one lane and cuts the old one.

34
00:02:10.233 --> 00:02:11.102
Quick check.

35
00:02:11.102 --> 00:02:17.620
Ten merchants, 100 milliseconds each, four lanes, and the lookup inside the returned flow.

36
00:02:17.620 --> 00:02:19.213
How long does it take?
